A hop crosses a boundary, and is recorded three times
A process running in the platform plane asks the sending tenant to perform
its half. The tenant does the work and sends the content directly to the
receiving tenant's ingress, which takes it; only a reference goes back to the
platform. The platform then records the hop itself: the participants, the
process it belongs to and the hashes of what moved, never the content. Three
records are written in three stores: the sender's egress and the receiver's
ingress in each tenant's own trail, and the coordination in the platform's.
